# B1 task job, far: T1 (forward and offline sweeps, the D_q arms, controls C1 to C3, S_k) and T2 (every
# restore and reverse arm and control) plus the position-resolved path patching, on all 100 held-out ids.
# Direction instructed-route, phase B1 (plans/B1-plan.md sections 0, 3, 4 and 5 ticket 7; spec.md R1).
# Each line composes the grid C_t exactly as mechanism-analysis jobs/05-p3-<task>.batch does (its --circuit,
# --expr Ct=..., --compose-granularity leaf, --reference and --task-from flags, copied verbatim), so the cell's
# Component set equals phase3/ct.json C_t for the task (far 72, ser 78; tests/test_instructed_route_b1_jobs.py).
# Held-out sample: the 100 ids of phase1/groups/<task>_heldout_D_sample.json (--include-ids, --n-causal 100).
# --route-ct names ct.json explicitly; the deciding set is <task>_heldout_D.json:greedy_k20 (20 Components).
# Path patching is on by default (--route-path-patching on). Written for B1 ticket 7; no generator script.
# Run from the repo root:  python analyze_components.py batch docs/research/instructed-route/jobs/B1-far.batch --timings outputs/_analyses/instructed-route-b1/timings/far.json
# Login check:            python analyze_components.py batch docs/research/instructed-route/jobs/B1-far.batch --dry-run

